  {"id":"lg-register-writing-task2","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Writing Task 2 语域指导","content":{"guidanceType":"register_note","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Writing Task 2 要求 academic/semi-formal/neutral 语域。生成例句和搭配时应避免过于口语化表达（gonna, wanna, stuff, a lot of），优先使用中性或学术表述。但不要求绝对正式，第一人称和适度的半正式表达可以接受。","examples":["It is widely acknowledged that...","A significant proportion of...","This can be attributed to..."],"antiExamples":["Lots of people think...","It's like really bad...","Stuff like pollution..."]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["register","writing","task2"]},
  {"id":"lg-register-writing-task1","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Writing Task 1 语域指导","content":{"guidanceType":"register_note","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task1"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Writing Task 1 要求客观中性语域。描述数据趋势时使用准确的动词和副词，避免主观评价和个人观点。","examples":["increased significantly","remained stable","accounted for approximately"],"antiExamples":["I think the graph shows...","It's obvious that..."]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["register","writing","task1"]},
  {"id":"lg-appropriacy-speaking","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Speaking 用词适切度指导","content":{"guidanceType":"appropriacy_rule","appliesTo":{"contexts":["speaking-part1","speaking-part2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Speaking 中可使用中性到半正式语域。Part 1 允许较自然口语；Part 3 可偏学术但需自然。词卡搭配和例句应体现口语中自然使用方式。","examples":["To be honest, I reckon...","From my perspective...","What strikes me is..."],"antiExamples":["It is widely acknowledged that... (过于书面)","The aforementioned... (过于正式)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["appropriacy","speaking","register"]},
  {"id":"lg-collocation-guidance","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"搭配生成指导","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"topics":["environment","technology","society","education","health","economy","government","globalisation","media","crime","transport","food","housing","arts","work","travel","family","science"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"生成 collocations 时应选择在学术写作和口语讨论中真实常见的搭配。每个词卡提供 3-5 个搭配，覆盖动词+名词、形容词+名词、副词+动词等多种模式。","examples":["mitigate the effects of...","pose a significant threat","address the underlying causes"],"antiExamples":["mitigate the thing (过于泛化)","very mitigate (语法错误)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["collocation","writing","speaking"]},
  {"id":"lg-paraphrase-guidance","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"同义替换策略指导","content":{"guidanceType":"paraphrase_strategy","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"词卡的 commonMistake 和 usageContext 应提示该词可以替换哪些常见表达。Lexical Resource 高分要求有效的同义替换。注意替换时含义精确匹配。","examples":["mitigate 可替换 reduce/lessen/alleviate","ubiquitous 可替换 widespread/pervasive"],"antiExamples":["mitigate = stop (含义偏差，mitigate 是减轻非消除)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["paraphrase","writing","speaking","lexical-resource"]},
  {"id":"lg-cause-effect","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"因果关系搭配模式","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"因果关系是 IELTS 写作和口语中最常见的逻辑关系。词卡如涉及因果关系词汇，应在搭配和例句中体现因果表达模式。","examples":["give rise to","result in","stem from","be attributed to","lead to"],"antiExamples":["make something happen (过于简单)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["collocation","cause-effect","writing","speaking"]},
  {"id":"lg-comparison-contrast","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"比较与对比搭配模式","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"比较对比结构在 IELTS 议论文和 Part 3 讨论中频繁出现。相关词汇的搭配应体现比较关系。","examples":["in contrast to","outweigh","whereas","on the other hand","compared with"],"antiExamples":["is more better than (语法错误)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["collocation","comparison","writing","speaking"]},
  {"id":"lg-opinion-expression","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"观点表达搭配模式","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"表达观点时应使用多样化的引入方式，避免反复使用 I think。","examples":["from my perspective","it seems to me that","I am convinced that","one could argue that"],"antiExamples":["I think (过度重复)","in my opinion I think (冗余)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["collocation","opinion","writing","speaking"]},
  {"id":"lg-hedging-writing","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"学术写作中 hedging 表达","content":{"guidanceType":"idiomatic_usage","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"学术写作中避免过于绝对的表述，使用 hedging 表达（可能、倾向于、在一定程度上）体现学术严谨。","examples":["tend to","it is likely that","to some extent","arguably"],"antiExamples":["always","never","definitely (过于绝对)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["hedging","writing","academic","register"]},
  {"id":"lg-exemplification","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"举例论证搭配模式","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"举例是论证和独白中必不可少的手段。词卡应在搭配或 usageContext 中体现举例表达。","examples":["for instance","a case in point is","this is exemplified by","take...as an example"],"antiExamples":["like (过于口语，写作中避免)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["exemplification","writing","speaking"]},
  {"id":"lg-concession","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"让步与转折搭配模式","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"让步转折是展示论证深度的关键手段。相关词汇应在搭配中体现让步逻辑。","examples":["nevertheless","notwithstanding","albeit","while it is true that","having said that"],"antiExamples":["but (单独使用过于简单)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["concession","writing","speaking","coherence"]},
  {"id":"lg-idiomatic-speaking","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Speaking 中适度习语使用","content":{"guidanceType":"idiomatic_usage","appliesTo":{"contexts":["speaking-part1","speaking-part2","speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Speaking 中适度使用习语（idioms）可体现词汇丰富度，但不宜过度堆砌。词卡如为习语类表达，应说明自然使用的语境。","examples":["a blessing in disguise","take something for granted","the tip of the iceberg"],"antiExamples":["连续使用 3 个以上习语（不自然）"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["idiom","speaking","vocabulary"]},
  {"id":"lg-appropriacy-speaking-p1","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Speaking Part 1 简短回答指导","content":{"guidanceType":"appropriacy_rule","appliesTo":{"contexts":["speaking-part1"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Part 1 回答应自然简短（2-4句），不需要展示过于学术的词汇。词卡在 Part 1 语境下的搭配和例句应体现日常交流风格。","examples":["To be honest, I quite enjoy...","I'd say I'm more of a...","Not really, I tend to..."],"antiExamples":["It is widely acknowledged that... (Part 1 中不自然)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["speaking","part1","appropriacy"]},
  {"id":"lg-appropriacy-speaking-p3","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"Speaking Part 3 深入讨论指导","content":{"guidanceType":"appropriacy_rule","appliesTo":{"contexts":["speaking-part3"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"Part 3 允许使用更学术的表达，但需保持口语自然度。词卡在 Part 3 语境下应体现抽象讨论中的自然用法。","examples":["I'd argue that...","One possible explanation is...","From a broader perspective..."],"antiExamples":["The aforementioned hypothesis... (书面感过强)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["speaking","part3","appropriacy"]},
  {"id":"lg-quantification","type":"lexical_guidance","title":"量化与程度表达指导","content":{"guidanceType":"collocation_pattern","appliesTo":{"contexts":["writing-task1","writing-task2"],"itemTypes":["WORD","PHRASE","CHUNK"]},"guidance":"写作中需要准确量化或表达程度。词卡涉及程度/量化时应提供对应搭配。","examples":["a significant proportion","the vast majority","to a certain extent","marginally higher"],"antiExamples":["a lot of (口语化)","very very big (非学术)"]},"provenance":{"sourceType":"project_authored","sourceId":"lexical-guidance-v1","sourceTitle":"词卡生成教学指导规则 V1","updatedAt":"2026-08-09"},"tags":["quantification","writing","task1","task2"]}
]
